<!--
    kuna issue testcase: on an Apple AArch64 image a callee whose own body runs
    va_start is variadic at its call sites (`option darwinvarargs on|off`,
    default-ON).

    Issue:      an iOS 16.4.1 kernelcache rendered
                `panic("NULL vnode passed to vnode_initialize @%s:%d");` while
                the caller stores both arguments with `stp x8, x9, [sp]`.
                Apple's arm64 ABI passes every variadic argument on the stack
                from [sp]; `varargstackargs` scores that tail only for a callee
                whose prototype says `...`, and nothing declares panic.
    Stage:      P4 active-input trial scoring (`p4_calls/kuna_darwinvarargs.rs`
                marks the callee from its entry block: Apple's va_start keeps
                the address entry-sp + 0 in a variable).
    P0 assert:  `option darwinvarargs on|off`.

    The XML wrapper only provides the harness architecture.  Every pass clears
    it and loads `darwinvarargs_macho_arm64` (arm64 Mach-O) or
    `darwinvarargs_aarch64` (AArch64 ELF), both built from `darwinvarargs.c`
    beside them.  `_check` calls `_report(fmt, file, line)`, whose body runs
    va_start, with file and line stored at [sp] and [sp+8], and calls
    `_sum9`, a non-variadic callee whose ninth argument is on the stack.

    Pass 1 (Mach-O, `option darwinvarargs off`) reproduces the bug: the call
    keeps only its format string.
    Pass 2 (Mach-O, shipped default) recovers both stack arguments.
    Pass 3 (ELF, shipped default): AAPCS64 passes the variadic arguments in
    x1 and x2, and the call reads them there as before.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c0035fd6
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
